{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791633099,"nonce":"4LJzqh0/J5uu5Qc648jgG1gEy8I=","message":"Text areas and selects now take part in constraints: 2bfeb5a0177bbfe0446894d5e66e0cd0e4e27820. FormControl is what a Form gathers; Input, TextArea and Select implement it. A TextArea takes name, required, minlength and maxlength; a Select takes required, invalid while its value is empty. Both keep the form states CSS reads.\n\n**Left: table rowspan**\nTaffy 0.14 still has no display: contents, and every row is its own grid. Two ways:\n- Rows as fragments, which LayoutTree already lays out in their parent's place, so all cells share one table grid and a cell spans rows with grid-row: span N. Rows then have no box, so a row's background (striping, hover) must be painted on its cells.\n- Rows stay grids. Each cell's column is placed from HTML's table algorithm, skipping slots taken by spans from rows above, and a spanning cell is sized to the rows it covers after a layout pass, which needs a second pass.","files":null}]}